WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.970
Australia's Great Barrier Reef is reported
to contribute 9 billion dollars a year

2
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.530
to the economy.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.530
Many drugs are now being developed
from reef animals and plants.

4
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.090
Only about half the CO₂ people
emit each year stays in the air.

5
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:18.490
Land ecosystems and
oceans absorb the rest.

6
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.030
Nature gives all of this for free.

7
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.650
So why do we keep cutting forests down?

8
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.730
Does nobody know what they give us?

9
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:30.650
In this mission, you'll sort what
nature gives us into goods and services.

10
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.490
Then you'll weigh the trade-offs
when people use an ecosystem.

11
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.570
Your mission: explain why people keep
clearing ecosystems that give so much for

12
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.200
free.
